# Reaction Docker Quick Run

Run everything from the project root (`Reaction-v4`).

## Build image

docker build -t reaction-v4 .

## Prepare runs folder permissions (important)

mkdir -p runs
sudo chown -R "$(id -u):$(id -g)" runs

## Optional: GPU check (only if host has NVIDIA runtime)

docker run --rm --gpus all nvidia/cuda:11.8.0-base-ubuntu22.04 nvidia-smi


## Problem with compute overlap

   docker run --rm -v "$(pwd):/host" reaction-v4 \
     sh -c 'cp /app/compute_overlap.cpython-*.so /host/ 2>/dev/null || true'

     ------------------ (CPU-only, VPN/host networking) ------------------

## 1) Video

docker run --rm \
  --network host \
  -u "$(id -u):$(id -g)" \
  -v "$(pwd)/runs:/app/runs" \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  reaction.py --video --vpn-kafka

##  2) USB camera /dev/video0

docker run --rm \
  --network host \
  --device /dev/video0:/dev/video0 \
  --group-add "$(getent group video | cut -d: -f3)" \
  -u "$(id -u):$(id -g)" \
  -v "$(pwd)/runs:/app/runs" \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  reaction.py --usb-cam --vpn-kafka --model land


## 3) Live Stream		

docker run --rm \
  --network host \
  --device /dev/video0:/dev/video0 \
  --group-add "$(getent group video | cut -d: -f3)" \
  -u "$(id -u):$(id -g)" \
  -v "$(pwd)/runs:/app/runs" \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  reaction.py --stream --vpn-kafka --model land



## 4) Run telemetry test producer

docker run --rm --network host \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  functions/test/producer_telemetry.py


## 5) Run test consumer

 docker run --rm --network host \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  functions/test/consumer.py --topic ObjectDetection



        --------------------- (With GPU, VPN/host networking) -----------------------------
             
             

docker rm -f reaction-rtsp 2>/dev/null; docker run --rm \
  --name reaction-rtsp \
  --gpus all \
  --network host \
  -u "$(id -u):$(id -g)" \
  -v "$(pwd):/app" \
  -v "$(pwd)/runs:/app/runs" \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  reaction.py --stream --vpn-kafka --model land --drone-name SIM_Alpha


# Τι τρέχει / GPU
docker ps --filter name=reaction-
nvidia-smi



  ---------------------  CLI arguments reference   --------------------- 

All flags for `reaction.py` (defaults from `functions/config.json` unless noted):

--usb-cam [/dev/videoN]   # USB camera input; optional device path (default: usb_cam_device in config)
--video                   # Local video file from config (video_input_path)
--video-path PATH         # Local video file path; overrides video_input_path (e.g. video_input/7shield_1.mp4)
--stream                  # RTSP stream from config (rtsp_link)
--vpn-kafka               # Use VPN Kafka broker (broker_vpn) instead of public broker

--save-frames             # Save annotated frames under runs/<timestamp>/frames/
--save-video              # Save annotated MP4 under runs/<timestamp>/video/
--save-json               # Save detection JSON under runs/<timestamp>/json/ (Kafka sends regardless)

--drone-name NAME         # Filter UAV_Telemetry by drone name (default: accept all)
--drone-id N              # Filter UAV_Telemetry by drone id (default: accept all)
--polygon                 # Enable polygon/NFZ gating; detection runs only inside allowed area

--detection-fps [N]         # Max inference rate (frames/sec); 0 = no limit; stream uses timer + fresh frame
--sampling [N]              # Send to Kafka every N-th detected frame (current frame only; 1 = every detection)
--info [N]                # Terminal [Infer]/[Kafka] every N detections (--info = 100; --info 1 = all); enables rate stats
--raw-detections          # Skip DeepSORT; send model boxes immediately (sync test mode)
--kafka-delay SEC         # Pause SEC seconds after each Kafka send; 0 = no pause (default: 0)
--model {land,sea}        # Model preset: land (736²) or sea (640²); sets model_path, labels, input size

--quiet                   # Less terminal output; logs still written under runs/<timestamp>/
--verbose                 # Extra per-detection logs (class, confidence, track id)
--test-stream             # Write stream diagnostics to runs/<timestamp>/test-stream

Example (RTSP, raw detections, 1 infer/sec, no kafka delay):

docker run --rm \
  --network host \
  -v "$(pwd):/app" \
  -v "$(pwd)/runs:/app/runs" \
  --entrypoint python3 \
  reaction-v4 \
  reaction.py --stream --vpn-kafka --model land --drone-name SIM_Alpha \
    --detection-fps 1 --raw-detections --kafka-delay 0


